{"response": {"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "Here are some great ways to pass the time while waiting for a flight at the airport:\n\n**Relax and Recharge**\n* **Access an airport lounge:** Even if you aren't flying first class, you can often buy a day pass to a lounge for comfortable seating, free food, Wi-Fi, and sometimes even showers.\n* **Get a massage:** Many large airports have spa kiosks (like XpresSpa) where you can get a quick neck, back, or foot massage.\n* **Meditate or find a quiet zone:** Some airports have designated quiet rooms, yoga rooms, or interfaith chapels that are perfect for escaping the noise.\n\n**Entertainment**\n* **Download shows and movies:** Use the airport Wi-Fi to download a few episodes of a show or a movie to your phone or tablet before you get on the plane.\n* **Listen to a podcast or audiobook:** Throw on some noise-canceling headphones and dive into a good story while you wait.\n* **Bring a good book:** Airports are one of the best places to read. If you forgot a book, browse the airport bookstores for a new bestseller. \n\n**Stay Active**\n* **Go for a walk:** You are about to be sitting for a long time. Walk from one end of the terminal to the other to get your steps in and stretch your legs. \n* **People-watch:** Airports offer some of the best people-watching in the world. Grab a coffee, find a seat facing the concourse, and watch the world go by.\n\n**Productivity and Planning**\n* **Catch up on life admin:** Use the time to clear out your email inbox, organize the photos on your phone, or pay some bills.\n* **Plan your itinerary:** If you are heading on vacation, use the extra time to look up restaurants, map out sightseeing routes, or book tickets for tours at your destination.\n\n**Food and Shopping**\n* **Have a nice meal:** Skip the fast food and find a sit-down restaurant. Treating yourself to a leisurely meal or a drink at the bar can easily eat up an hour or two.\n* **Browse Duty-Free:** Even if you aren't planning to buy anything, wandering through the duty-free shops to smell the colognes or look at luxury goods is a classic way to kill time.", "thoughtSignature": ""}], "role": "model"}, "finishReason": "STOP", "index": 0}], "usageMetadata": {"promptTokenCount": 29, "candidatesTokenCount": 489, "totalTokenCount": 783, "promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT", "tokenCount": 29}], "thoughtsTokenCount": 265, "serviceTier": "standard"}, "modelVersion": "gemini-3.1-pro-preview", "responseId": "ABnHavOnLamr_PUPvMSLmQE"}, "metadata": {"key": "7b3cb48202768bd155817c3b256fdc70a4d4df3931b4586b61ab0ca3414cebd7"}}
